1
00:00:10,914 --> 00:00:16,106
A 30-story luxury condominium under construction

2
00:00:16,130 --> 00:00:17,981
has collapsed.

3
00:00:18,071 --> 00:00:18,938
As for the cause,

4
00:00:19,375 --> 00:00:21,551
volunteer engineers have raised concerns

5
00:00:21,575 --> 00:00:23,008
about the strength of the main pillars

6
00:00:23,032 --> 00:00:24,429
and the quality of the concrete.

7
00:00:24,775 --> 00:00:27,910
Construction errors may have caused the collapse.

8
00:00:27,934 --> 00:00:31,644
Mr. C was the engineer in charge of the project.

9
00:00:31,879 --> 00:00:35,457
An official investigation is still pending.

10
00:00:35,992 --> 00:00:39,624
There are reportedly many injured and dead.

11
00:00:39,736 --> 00:00:43,309
Most of the workers were migrant laborers.

12
00:00:43,788 --> 00:00:47,784
Rescue teams are continuing their search

13
00:00:47,808 --> 00:00:50,615
for people trapped beneath the rubble.

14
00:01:05,903 --> 00:01:08,420
Hello. Welcome to Sunny Mart.

15
00:01:18,011 --> 00:01:18,993
What was that?

16
00:01:19,415 --> 00:01:20,016
Huh?

17
00:01:31,927 --> 00:01:32,561
Help!

18
00:01:36,596 --> 00:01:37,417
Help me!

19
00:01:37,614 --> 00:01:38,419
Help me!

20
00:01:38,734 --> 00:01:40,340
Something's chasing me!

21
00:01:40,704 --> 00:01:41,534
Help me!

22
00:01:43,200 --> 00:01:45,238
You have to pay for your own sins.

23
00:01:47,003 --> 00:01:49,446
I didn't do it. I didn't mean to.

24
00:01:49,878 --> 00:01:51,232
I didn't mean to do it.

25
00:01:52,086 --> 00:01:53,708
I'll do anything you want.

26
00:01:53,830 --> 00:01:56,556
I'll do anything. Please help me!

27
00:01:57,564 --> 00:01:59,681
Then how about becoming the store manager?

28
00:02:02,787 --> 00:02:04,184
What are you talking about?

29
00:02:04,851 --> 00:02:07,085
This job will make people forget your past.

30
00:02:07,181 --> 00:02:08,653
And it will buy you some time.

31
00:02:17,855 --> 00:02:19,791
Become the store manager?

32
00:02:20,081 --> 00:02:20,999
If it'll help me...

33
00:02:21,340 --> 00:02:21,916
I'll do it.

34
00:02:24,089 --> 00:02:27,319
Remember the rules are as important as your life.

35
00:03:35,129 --> 00:03:36,532
Every night-shift employee

36
00:03:37,071 --> 00:03:38,778
who works the night shift at Sunny Mart

37
00:03:39,887 --> 00:03:41,978
has something they need to atone for.

38
00:03:44,565 --> 00:03:45,482
But wait, Cherd.

39
00:03:47,995 --> 00:03:48,971
When you said

40
00:03:49,702 --> 00:03:51,382
that becoming the store manager

41
00:03:54,395 --> 00:03:56,097
would make people forget our past,

42
00:03:57,014 --> 00:03:58,070
what exactly did you mean?

43
00:03:58,390 --> 00:03:59,243
Just what I said.

44
00:03:59,702 --> 00:04:00,486
As I explained,

45
00:04:01,531 --> 00:04:02,608
if you become the store manager,

46
00:04:03,211 --> 00:04:04,358
people will forget you.

47
00:04:04,438 --> 00:04:05,563
They'll forget what you did.

48
00:04:06,596 --> 00:04:07,135
Everything.

49
00:04:10,500 --> 00:04:12,265
Doesn't that sound a little far-fetched?

50
00:04:14,771 --> 00:04:15,427
Far-fetched?

51
00:04:17,288 --> 00:04:18,302
Metha.

52
00:04:19,256 --> 00:04:20,008
Just look around.

53
00:04:20,296 --> 00:04:21,523
In this store,

54
00:04:23,286 --> 00:04:25,543
there are plenty of things in this store

55
00:04:25,649 --> 00:04:26,796
that defy expectations.

56
00:04:28,425 --> 00:04:30,581
And look at the rules and conditions this store uses

57
00:04:30,606 --> 00:04:31,581
to choose its employees.

58
00:04:32,634 --> 00:04:33,599
Come to think of it.

59
00:04:34,954 --> 00:04:35,951
Fate.

60
00:04:36,895 --> 00:04:37,546
Something like that.

61
00:04:44,205 --> 00:04:44,829
Then...

62
00:04:45,832 --> 00:04:46,584
Fate

63
00:04:52,072 --> 00:04:53,763
must have brought all of us together.

64
00:04:56,616 --> 00:04:57,656
Pork dumplings.

65
00:04:59,852 --> 00:05:01,281
I really like these.

66
00:05:03,273 --> 00:05:04,034
You know me so well.

67
00:05:04,058 --> 00:05:06,081
How did you know I love pork dumplings?

68
00:05:15,455 --> 00:05:16,735
You like them that much?

69
00:05:18,111 --> 00:05:18,463
Here.

70
00:05:20,063 --> 00:05:21,162
You can have two.

71
00:05:21,547 --> 00:05:22,016
What?

72
00:05:29,940 --> 00:05:31,300
I haven't had these

73
00:05:32,372 --> 00:05:33,194
in a long time.

74
00:05:36,111 --> 00:05:37,236
The dumplings, you mean?

75
00:05:39,092 --> 00:05:39,738
No.

76
00:05:40,505 --> 00:05:41,283
I mean

77
00:05:42,089 --> 00:05:44,016
I haven't sat down and shared a meal

78
00:05:44,040 --> 00:05:45,630
with other people like this

79
00:05:47,982 --> 00:05:48,638
in a long time.

80
00:05:49,916 --> 00:05:51,490
I can't even remember the last time.

81
00:06:00,246 --> 00:06:00,806
Then...

82
00:06:01,051 --> 00:06:02,896
Maybe we should go out for a meal sometime.

83
00:06:06,347 --> 00:06:08,070
I never see you leave the store, Cherd.

84
00:06:08,979 --> 00:06:09,528
Let's go.

85
00:06:14,286 --> 00:06:15,176
I can't, Dear.

86
00:06:16,966 --> 00:06:18,022
The manager of this store

87
00:06:19,035 --> 00:06:20,395
isn't allowed to leave.

88
00:06:21,654 --> 00:06:22,427
It's a rule.

89
00:06:33,593 --> 00:06:34,782
You're such a downer.

90
00:06:36,255 --> 00:06:37,866
I've told you everything about me.

91
00:06:38,778 --> 00:06:39,716
Now tell me about yourself.

92
00:06:40,405 --> 00:06:41,402
Tell me.

93
00:06:42,513 --> 00:06:46,679
How did fate bring you to this night-shift job?

94
00:06:50,625 --> 00:06:51,868
My story?

95
00:06:54,695 --> 00:06:55,617
That was a long time ago.

96
00:07:30,318 --> 00:07:31,854
See? I told you.

97
00:07:32,329 --> 00:07:33,369
It's easy.

98
00:07:47,927 --> 00:07:49,234
Have you chosen yet, kid?

99
00:08:01,996 --> 00:08:02,636
Five baht.

100
00:08:21,702 --> 00:08:22,369
Wait.

101
00:08:41,130 --> 00:08:42,469
This one's on me.

102
00:09:04,599 --> 00:09:05,666
Excuse me.

103
00:09:05,821 --> 00:09:07,442
I can't reach that one.

104
00:09:12,635 --> 00:09:14,214
Is it too high?

105
00:09:16,214 --> 00:09:16,971
Which one?

106
00:09:17,558 --> 00:09:18,156
That one.

107
00:09:20,131 --> 00:09:20,951
Which one, dear?

108
00:09:21,187 --> 00:09:22,045
Over there.

109
00:09:22,200 --> 00:09:23,293
Oh, okay.

110
00:09:26,669 --> 00:09:27,949
Which one, dear?

111
00:09:28,528 --> 00:09:29,414
This one?

112
00:09:29,738 --> 00:09:30,837
The one next to it.

113
00:09:30,861 --> 00:09:32,072
Oh, another one. Okay.

114
00:09:32,379 --> 00:09:33,424
This one, right?

115
00:09:36,230 --> 00:09:37,243
What about that one?

116
00:09:37,684 --> 00:09:40,303
Oh, another one? Further inside?

117
00:09:42,217 --> 00:09:43,070
This one?

118
00:09:46,344 --> 00:09:47,283
Not that one either?

119
00:09:47,415 --> 00:09:48,705
That one!

120
00:09:49,715 --> 00:09:50,739
Another one?

121
00:09:51,430 --> 00:09:53,345
This one? That one over there.

122
00:09:54,761 --> 00:09:56,651
The one behind it? Here you go.

123
00:09:57,231 --> 00:09:58,633
Another one?

124
00:10:00,361 --> 00:10:02,276
This one? Okay, this one, right?

125
00:10:03,951 --> 00:10:06,345
Hey, kid! What are you doing?

126
00:10:07,268 --> 00:10:07,924
Den!

127
00:10:10,553 --> 00:10:11,369
Uncle.

128
00:10:12,004 --> 00:10:13,028
I told you to get out!

129
00:10:13,174 --> 00:10:13,798
Hurry!

130
00:10:13,822 --> 00:10:14,991
Uncle fell because of Dear.

131
00:10:15,016 --> 00:10:16,368
Get out! Now!

132
00:10:19,355 --> 00:10:21,483
I heard he slipped and hit his head.

133
00:10:21,631 --> 00:10:22,809
What a shame.

134
00:10:22,916 --> 00:10:24,431
He didn't have any family to look after him.

135
00:10:24,532 --> 00:10:24,932
Yeah.

136
00:10:25,165 --> 00:10:26,647
I saw him just this morning.

137
00:10:26,671 --> 00:10:28,122
He was carrying things around.

138
00:10:36,014 --> 00:10:36,628
Dear.

139
00:10:40,263 --> 00:10:41,628
Stop crying.

140
00:10:44,717 --> 00:10:45,672
Den.

141
00:10:46,407 --> 00:10:48,162
I killed someone.

142
00:10:50,640 --> 00:10:51,845
We're not going to talk about this.

143
00:10:52,544 --> 00:10:53,914
We're never doing anything like that again.

144
00:10:54,522 --> 00:10:55,514
Promise me.

145
00:10:57,931 --> 00:10:59,221
I think

146
00:11:00,201 --> 00:11:01,689
maybe this is my karma.

147
00:11:06,596 --> 00:11:07,529
But it's strange.

148
00:11:09,879 --> 00:11:11,591
I've never seen Uncle Phet here.

149
00:11:16,274 --> 00:11:17,575
You could look at it this way.

150
00:11:18,133 --> 00:11:19,125
Maybe

151
00:11:19,856 --> 00:11:20,416
he had

152
00:11:21,808 --> 00:11:23,786
no unfinished business left.

153
00:11:25,707 --> 00:11:27,205
Maybe he was just

154
00:11:28,860 --> 00:11:29,634
waiting for his time.

155
00:11:34,647 --> 00:11:36,210
Then what about you, Metha?

156
00:11:36,476 --> 00:11:37,698
Have you settled your debt too?

157
00:11:41,853 --> 00:11:42,365
Yeah.

158
00:11:43,463 --> 00:11:44,551
I think it's over.

159
00:11:47,495 --> 00:11:48,306
That's good.

160
00:11:50,012 --> 00:11:51,239
Because if it isn't,

161
00:11:52,337 --> 00:11:53,697
no matter how far we run,

162
00:11:54,858 --> 00:11:55,770
we can't escape it.

163
00:12:56,860 --> 00:12:58,013
What is that noise?

164
00:14:29,488 --> 00:14:30,347
(Are you ready?)

165
00:14:30,433 --> 00:14:31,708
(Let's go Nava)

166
00:15:39,757 --> 00:15:40,498
Metha.

167
00:15:43,824 --> 00:15:45,218
That's the third time you've put dish soap

168
00:15:45,242 --> 00:15:46,566
in the snack aisle.

169
00:15:50,998 --> 00:15:51,750
Sorry.

170
00:15:57,870 --> 00:15:58,846
Is everything okay?

171
00:16:04,458 --> 00:16:04,964
Dear.

172
00:16:06,965 --> 00:16:08,027
Have you ever run into

173
00:16:08,073 --> 00:16:09,541
any of those customers outside the store?

174
00:16:11,916 --> 00:16:13,068
Outside the store?

175
00:16:14,908 --> 00:16:15,537
I don't know.

176
00:16:15,996 --> 00:16:17,298
I don't really pay attention.

177
00:16:18,215 --> 00:16:18,881
But if I ever do,

178
00:16:19,206 --> 00:16:20,785
I'd rather meet them inside the store.

179
00:16:21,799 --> 00:16:22,290
Why?

180
00:16:23,468 --> 00:16:25,751
At least if we're inside the store

181
00:16:26,146 --> 00:16:27,047
and follow the rules,

182
00:16:27,415 --> 00:16:28,690
we still have a chance to survive.

183
00:16:31,247 --> 00:16:31,769
That's true.

184
00:16:33,497 --> 00:16:34,617
Did you see something?

185
00:16:36,324 --> 00:16:36,836
No.

186
00:17:21,659 --> 00:17:22,582
Hello, Metha.

187
00:17:22,678 --> 00:17:23,686
Hello.

188
00:17:27,259 --> 00:17:27,830
Wow.

189
00:17:29,623 --> 00:17:30,540
You look like

190
00:17:30,679 --> 00:17:32,284
you haven't slept more than three hours.

191
00:17:34,076 --> 00:17:35,249
Something like that.

192
00:17:38,811 --> 00:17:40,619
You've lasted quite a while here.

193
00:17:42,277 --> 00:17:42,949
That's good, bro.

194
00:17:43,691 --> 00:17:45,051
At least I'll have someone to talk to.

195
00:17:47,024 --> 00:17:47,776
What about you?

196
00:17:47,973 --> 00:17:49,082
Don't you ever think about changing jobs?

197
00:17:49,989 --> 00:17:50,741
No.

198
00:17:51,183 --> 00:17:52,474
I like being a delivery driver.

199
00:17:53,812 --> 00:17:55,146
I think it suits me better.

200
00:17:56,629 --> 00:17:59,498
I've tried sitting around at work,

201
00:17:59,525 --> 00:18:01,141
like watching a shop all day.

202
00:18:01,792 --> 00:18:02,618
I couldn't stand it.

203
00:18:02,837 --> 00:18:03,840
It felt like being in prison.

204
00:18:04,202 --> 00:18:04,922
You're exaggerating.

205
00:18:05,782 --> 00:18:06,454
I'm serious.

206
00:18:06,780 --> 00:18:08,583
Some people are better suited to jobs

207
00:18:08,689 --> 00:18:10,300
where they can keep moving around.

208
00:18:11,718 --> 00:18:12,540
Like me.

209
00:18:13,326 --> 00:18:14,190
A traveler.

210
00:18:32,550 --> 00:18:33,995
Wait, is this order wrong?

211
00:18:35,168 --> 00:18:36,827
We usually only sell the small size.

212
00:18:37,552 --> 00:18:38,374
It's not a mistake.

213
00:18:40,264 --> 00:18:41,779
They ordered it for this branch.

214
00:18:42,589 --> 00:18:43,907
A 15-kilogram bag.

215
00:18:45,059 --> 00:18:46,643
You can take the box for now.

216
00:19:34,012 --> 00:19:34,929
What's up, Metha?

217
00:19:35,126 --> 00:19:36,572
There's something I wanted to ask you.

218
00:19:43,016 --> 00:19:44,296
Let's go out front.

219
00:19:47,801 --> 00:19:48,361
Dear.

220
00:19:48,393 --> 00:19:51,428
When the lights turn red, employees have 15 minutes.

221
00:19:51,625 --> 00:19:52,047
Cherd.

222
00:19:52,190 --> 00:19:53,065
What should we do?

223
00:19:53,624 --> 00:19:55,246
I've never seen this rule before.

224
00:19:57,305 --> 00:19:59,033
Clear the middle of the store.

225
00:19:59,214 --> 00:19:59,694
Go!

226
00:19:59,989 --> 00:20:01,035
Go, go!

227
00:20:10,560 --> 00:20:13,517
Bring "meat" and place it in the middle of the store.

228
00:20:14,165 --> 00:20:15,456
Do not let the meat run out.

229
00:20:24,053 --> 00:20:26,437
Then light one incense stick.

230
00:20:28,150 --> 00:20:30,603
The incense must remain lit at all times.

231
00:20:30,658 --> 00:20:32,923
Do not let it go out until the situation is over.

232
00:20:37,670 --> 00:20:40,209
(Convenience Store Rules)

233
00:20:53,333 --> 00:20:55,482
Hello. Welcome to Sunny Mart.

234
00:21:23,000 --> 00:21:24,291
They're eating.

235
00:21:39,353 --> 00:21:39,924
What is it?

236
00:21:44,633 --> 00:21:45,086
Cherd!

237
00:21:45,486 --> 00:21:46,217
Why are you startled?

238
00:22:13,889 --> 00:22:14,721
What's happening?

239
00:22:24,958 --> 00:22:26,420
They're coming this way!

240
00:22:27,921 --> 00:22:28,439
Huh?

241
00:22:30,337 --> 00:22:31,185
What did you say?

242
00:22:31,964 --> 00:22:33,521
But we followed the rules, didn't we?

243
00:22:38,098 --> 00:22:40,375
(Convenience Store Rules)

244
00:22:47,177 --> 00:22:47,977
This is bad.

245
00:22:51,609 --> 00:22:52,793
The rules have changed.

246
00:22:58,889 --> 00:23:00,211
Hey! Dear, go!

247
00:23:09,878 --> 00:23:11,148
What do you mean the rules have changed?

248
00:23:11,511 --> 00:23:12,317
Yeah.

249
00:23:12,396 --> 00:23:13,372
Can the rules change?

250
00:23:13,772 --> 00:23:14,625
Don't forget.

251
00:23:15,292 --> 00:23:16,073
This store

252
00:23:16,861 --> 00:23:19,557
will do anything to lure us into breaking the rules,

253
00:23:20,160 --> 00:23:21,531
especially on a night like this.

254
00:23:22,779 --> 00:23:23,931
What are the new rules?

255
00:23:25,328 --> 00:23:27,212
Employees must not remain near the counter

256
00:23:27,237 --> 00:23:28,867
for more than three minutes.

257
00:23:29,719 --> 00:23:30,295
So...

258
00:23:31,057 --> 00:23:32,359
we're safe now, right?

259
00:23:32,839 --> 00:23:33,713
That's not all.

260
00:23:35,210 --> 00:23:37,973
Do not move when a customer is looking at you.

261
00:23:52,100 --> 00:23:53,803
Employees must not make any sound

262
00:23:53,828 --> 00:23:54,936
that customers can hear.

263
00:24:18,913 --> 00:24:19,243
Hey.

264
00:24:20,737 --> 00:24:21,297
They're gone.

265
00:24:31,152 --> 00:24:31,867
The incense is about to go out.

266
00:24:35,303 --> 00:24:37,511
Why is it burning out so quickly?

267
00:24:39,543 --> 00:24:40,282
I'll take it from here.

268
00:26:48,707 --> 00:26:49,869
We're running out of meat.

269
00:26:51,577 --> 00:26:52,190
Metha.

270
00:26:52,440 --> 00:26:53,112
We're running out of meat.

271
00:26:54,207 --> 00:26:55,930
And all we have left is canned food.

272
00:26:56,504 --> 00:26:58,109
They ordered a 15-kilogram bag of dog food

273
00:26:58,133 --> 00:26:59,847
for this branch.

274
00:27:01,164 --> 00:27:01,825
I'll be right back.

275
00:28:04,184 --> 00:28:05,230
Dog food?

276
00:28:05,875 --> 00:28:07,214
Since when do we stock that?

277
00:28:07,854 --> 00:28:08,531
It was delivered today.

278
00:28:08,915 --> 00:28:09,731
It should work.

279
00:28:59,504 --> 00:29:00,523
Over here!

280
00:29:00,837 --> 00:29:02,112
Hey! I'm here!

281
00:29:02,992 --> 00:29:05,046
Hey! Over here!

282
00:29:10,334 --> 00:29:10,905
Watch out!

283
00:29:39,929 --> 00:29:40,959
Are you okay?

284
00:29:48,303 --> 00:29:48,986
That was close.

285
00:29:49,476 --> 00:29:50,463
Well done, guys.

286
00:29:53,978 --> 00:29:55,439
So what exactly happened?

287
00:29:58,391 --> 00:30:00,812
When the lights in the store turn red,

288
00:30:01,581 --> 00:30:02,562
Sunny Mart

289
00:30:02,919 --> 00:30:04,205
becomes a place where free food is served.

290
00:30:04,653 --> 00:30:05,783
Homeless customers

291
00:30:06,188 --> 00:30:07,393
and customers who have no family

292
00:30:07,724 --> 00:30:10,108
can come in and eat for free.

293
00:30:11,073 --> 00:30:12,577
The customers on nights like this

294
00:30:12,994 --> 00:30:13,943
are really aggressive.

295
00:30:14,412 --> 00:30:15,708
They're more dangerous than usual.

296
00:30:16,188 --> 00:30:16,967
But thankfully,

297
00:30:18,140 --> 00:30:19,398
no matter what happens,

298
00:30:20,188 --> 00:30:21,244
following the rules

299
00:30:22,039 --> 00:30:23,692
is still our best protection.

300
00:30:24,602 --> 00:30:25,754
We got lucky.

301
00:30:26,298 --> 00:30:27,770
We all made it out alive.

302
00:30:28,266 --> 00:30:30,431
Lucky? What do you mean lucky?

303
00:30:30,996 --> 00:30:32,442
That was way too close.

304
00:30:32,996 --> 00:30:34,788
You were the only one wearing glasses,

305
00:30:35,247 --> 00:30:36,623
so you could see them.

306
00:30:37,866 --> 00:30:40,559
Do you know how hard it was for us?

307
00:30:42,719 --> 00:30:43,663
Come on.

308
00:30:44,388 --> 00:30:45,593
We're alive.

309
00:30:46,185 --> 00:30:47,364
Tonight's over.

310
00:30:55,274 --> 00:30:57,173
Why are the lights red again?

311
00:30:57,786 --> 00:30:59,024
They shouldn't turn red again.

312
00:30:59,172 --> 00:31:00,335
Does that mean it's not over?

313
00:31:06,201 --> 00:31:07,316
But we've run out of meat!

314
00:31:07,567 --> 00:31:08,665
What are we supposed to do?

315
00:31:10,319 --> 00:31:12,383
Hello. Welcome to Sunny Mart.

316
00:31:16,631 --> 00:31:17,826
They're here already?

317
00:31:18,162 --> 00:31:19,053
You can see them?

318
00:31:19,853 --> 00:31:21,394
I can see them perfectly.

319
00:31:22,248 --> 00:31:22,818
Dear!

320
00:31:22,957 --> 00:31:23,447
Metha!

321
00:31:23,847 --> 00:31:24,626
Get to the stockroom!

322
00:31:24,951 --> 00:31:25,858
Get to the stockroom!

323
00:31:27,399 --> 00:31:27,911
Hurry!

324
00:31:36,586 --> 00:31:38,255
Find something to block the door!

325
00:31:38,404 --> 00:31:39,449
Dear, move!

326
00:31:41,855 --> 00:31:42,490
Hurry!

327
00:31:43,401 --> 00:31:43,913
Help me push!

328
00:31:49,497 --> 00:31:50,265
Canned fish!

329
00:32:00,498 --> 00:32:02,343
This should work.

330
00:32:03,335 --> 00:32:04,380
Okay, okay!

331
00:32:06,310 --> 00:32:06,865
Cherd.

332
00:32:07,148 --> 00:32:07,846
Keep pushing.

333
00:32:11,956 --> 00:32:13,449
Dear, open these and put them in the bucket.

334
00:32:15,892 --> 00:32:17,924
Hurry! The door's about to break!

335
00:32:19,937 --> 00:32:20,380
Metha.

336
00:32:26,988 --> 00:32:28,887
This is so hard to open!

337
00:32:30,711 --> 00:32:32,663
Opening them one by one will take too long.

338
00:32:34,582 --> 00:32:36,225
Please help us.

339
00:32:36,354 --> 00:32:37,783
Help us.

340
00:32:39,783 --> 00:32:41,825
Hey, everyone! It's collapsing!

341
00:32:42,695 --> 00:32:43,666
Hurry! Run!

342
00:32:45,687 --> 00:32:46,642
Hey! Run!

343
00:32:48,060 --> 00:32:49,372
Watch out, everyone!

344
00:32:52,902 --> 00:32:53,472
Metha.

345
00:32:55,456 --> 00:32:57,115
It's time for me to pay.

346
00:32:58,267 --> 00:32:58,933
What are you talking about?

347
00:33:04,474 --> 00:33:05,759
But the metal is too thin.

348
00:33:07,162 --> 00:33:07,796
Yeah.

349
00:33:08,213 --> 00:33:09,834
If I say it'll work, it'll work.

350
00:33:15,263 --> 00:33:16,255
Get back to work.

351
00:33:17,498 --> 00:33:18,303
Why are you still here?

352
00:33:41,647 --> 00:33:42,388
Yes, sir.

353
00:33:43,055 --> 00:33:44,116
Don't worry, sir.

354
00:33:45,129 --> 00:33:46,814
I'll take care of everything just as you ordered.

355
00:33:49,750 --> 00:33:50,478
Understood.

356
00:33:51,305 --> 00:33:51,758
Yes.

357
00:33:53,330 --> 00:33:53,938
Yes, sir.

358
00:34:17,026 --> 00:34:17,660
Metha.

359
00:34:19,260 --> 00:34:20,188
Take these.

360
00:34:21,361 --> 00:34:21,953
What are you doing?

361
00:34:22,512 --> 00:34:23,778
Take the glasses.

362
00:34:25,426 --> 00:34:26,220
Take them!

363
00:34:31,885 --> 00:34:33,251
What are you doing?

364
00:34:33,592 --> 00:34:34,120
No!

365
00:34:35,016 --> 00:34:35,416
The rules...

366
00:34:36,861 --> 00:34:38,573
aren't just there to help us survive.

367
00:34:39,943 --> 00:34:41,191
They're there so we can pay for what we've done.

368
00:34:49,623 --> 00:34:50,142
Go!

369
00:34:50,733 --> 00:34:51,272
Cherd!

370
00:34:51,507 --> 00:34:52,745
Hey, Cherd!

371
00:34:53,192 --> 00:34:54,558
Cherd!

372
00:34:55,294 --> 00:34:56,078
Don't!

373
00:35:00,311 --> 00:35:01,772
You've been waiting a long time, haven't you?

374
00:35:10,180 --> 00:35:10,953
Cherd!

375
00:35:12,916 --> 00:35:14,409
If you want to eat, come and eat.

376
00:35:19,299 --> 00:35:20,254
No!

377
00:35:55,216 --> 00:35:56,992
With his potential, Dear,

378
00:35:57,260 --> 00:35:59,180
he might be able to handle the customers

379
00:35:59,281 --> 00:36:01,132
better than we expected.

380
00:36:01,546 --> 00:36:02,044
Here.

381
00:36:03,740 --> 00:36:04,620
This should cheer you up.

382
00:36:05,786 --> 00:36:06,852
My treat today.

383
00:36:08,100 --> 00:36:09,156
Pork dumplings.

384
00:36:09,620 --> 00:36:11,635
I haven't sat down and shared a meal

385
00:36:11,660 --> 00:36:13,166
with other people like this

386
00:36:14,958 --> 00:36:15,758
in a long time.

387
00:36:24,313 --> 00:36:27,428
This can't be real, can it?

388
00:37:04,751 --> 00:37:06,815
Cherd knew all along, didn't he?

389
00:37:09,898 --> 00:37:10,343
Yeah.

390
00:37:13,759 --> 00:37:14,661
He made his own choice.

391
00:37:17,470 --> 00:37:18,739
But this...

392
00:37:23,448 --> 00:37:24,264
Maybe...

393
00:37:28,032 --> 00:37:30,362
this was what Cherd really wanted

394
00:37:32,778 --> 00:37:34,074
when he talked about karma.

395
00:37:40,566 --> 00:37:42,662
What will happen to this store now?

396
00:37:45,972 --> 00:37:47,775
There's no store manager anymore.

397
00:39:03,830 --> 00:39:05,494
Dear, the store is completely closed.

398
00:39:05,537 --> 00:39:07,254
The lights are off, like no one's here.

399
00:39:07,602 --> 00:39:09,702
The store is closed because there's no manager.

400
00:39:10,000 --> 00:39:11,402
It might reopen

401
00:39:11,426 --> 00:39:13,036
when a new store manager is appointed.

402
00:39:13,276 --> 00:39:13,862
Metha.

403
00:39:14,129 --> 00:39:15,249
I think you should come back.

404
00:39:15,881 --> 00:39:16,729
Come back to the police.

405
00:39:17,860 --> 00:39:19,753
There's definitely something hidden in this store.

406
00:39:20,104 --> 00:39:22,233
And why are people like us drawn here?

407
00:39:22,314 --> 00:39:24,889
I have to find out what this place really is.

408
00:39:25,101 --> 00:39:25,743
Den!

409
00:39:26,077 --> 00:39:26,593
Den!

410
00:39:26,618 --> 00:39:27,230
Den!

411
00:39:30,943 --> 00:39:31,508
Den.
